GUI modernization, Phase 5 (fourth slice): search/sort/filter on the
Incidents page - execution order §9 Phase 5's own line, "Rebuild
Incidents (master/detail, search/sort/filter)". This slice is the
search/sort/filter half; master/detail (a distinct list+detail-panel
layout paradigm) is not attempted here - see §6 below for why.

## 1. The gap and why routing, not local state

The Incidents page listed every incident inline with no way to narrow a
long list down. `useRoute.ts`'s `InvestigationContext` (`query`/
`severities`/`families`/`sort`) has carried these exact fields since
Phase 3, documented as waiting for "each page's own Phase 3/5 rebuild" -
the same infrastructure `Evidence.tsx`'s incident-scoped export (the
previous slice) already started using for `from`/`to`/`selection`.
Filters live in the URL hash (not local `useState`, the way `Host.tsx`'s
search box does) deliberately: an investigation someone is filtering
down is worth bookmarking or sharing, unlike Host's quick one-off lookup.

## 2. What was built

`filterAndSortIncidents(incidents, context, rules, lang)` (new, exported
for direct testing): search matches the *translated* title (via the
same `findRule`/`titleFor` used everywhere else this session - typing an
Arabic phrase in Arabic mode must find the Arabic title containing it,
not silently search the raw English field nobody is looking at), plus
the always-technical `rule_id` and root-cause `entity`. Severity/family
filters are unset-safe (absent means "no filter", not "match nothing").
Three sort orders: newest (default), severity (error > warn > notice >
info, ISO 4217-style rank table), confidence - each with newest-first as
the tiebreaker.

`Incidents.tsx`: a search box (reusing the `.search-box` class `Host.tsx`
already established), a severity checkbox group, a family checkbox group
(built from the families actually present in this incident set - no
point offering a filter for a family with zero incidents), and a sort
`<select>`. Every control patches the route context via `navigate` and
re-renders from `filterAndSortIncidents`'s result - no separate draft
state to keep in sync. A distinct `incidents_no_matches` empty state
("no incidents match the current filters") from the pre-existing
`incidents_empty` ("no incidents in this window at all") - a filter
finding nothing and a genuinely quiet recording are different facts, and
conflating them would be exactly the "absence looks like nothing
happened" failure this whole project exists to avoid elsewhere.

